          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mtiuqlyanomih9p0",
          "message": {
            "text": "The shared opener must fail closed when no interactive TTY is attached. Environment sentinels alone were insufficient because automated pueue/Codex commands can invoke svg-scrubber or SVG Demo Test Review without VITEST or DOMOTIONNOOPEN, reusing the user’s running desktop Chrome. Interactive terminals retain the normal auto-open behavior; deliberately non-interactive human launchers may opt in with DOMOTIONOPENBROWSER=1, while VITEST, DOMOTIONNOOPEN, and CI always win.",
            "markdown": "The shared opener must fail closed when no interactive TTY is attached. Environment sentinels alone were insufficient because automated pueue/Codex commands can invoke svg-scrubber or SVG Demo Test Review without VITEST or DOMOTION_NO_OPEN, reusing the user’s running desktop Chrome. Interactive terminals retain the normal auto-open behavior; deliberately non-interactive human launchers may opt in with DOMOTION_OPEN_BROWSER=1, while VITEST, DOMOTION_NO_OPEN, and CI always win."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/cli/common.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 74,
                  "endLine": 91,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "export function shouldOpenInBrowser(\n  env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv = process.env,\n  interactive = Boolean(process.stdin.isTTY && process.stdout.isTTY),\n): boolean {\n  if (env.VITEST != null || env.DOMOTION_NO_OPEN === \"1\" || env.CI != null) return false;\n  return interactive || env.DOMOTION_OPEN_BROWSER === \"1\";\n}\n\nexport async function openInBrowser(url: string): Promise<void> {\n  // Test code must never steal focus by launching the user's real browser.\n  // Keep this guard here, at the final shared side-effect boundary, so a new\n  // caller cannot bypass it by forgetting its own `--no-open` flag. Vitest\n  // exports VITEST to its workers and their inherited child processes;\n  // DOMOTION_NO_OPEN covers other automated runners, and the TTY requirement\n  // fails closed for pueue/Codex/CI-style commands that carry neither sentinel.\n  // A deliberately non-interactive human launcher can opt in with\n  // DOMOTION_OPEN_BROWSER=1 (unless an automation/no-open sentinel is present).\n  if (!shouldOpenInBrowser()) return;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
